# Cluster

Used to cluster child elements in a wrap-able horizontal row.

Adding a `.u-flex-grow` class, or flex-grow CSS rule to a child element will cause it to stretch to fill available space.

## Useage

```html
<div class="l-cluster">
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	...
</div>

```

## Default

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-cluster">
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Custom properties

| Property name           | Default value |
| ----------------------- | ------------- |
| `--cluster-space--component`          | `var(--s-1)`  |
| `--cluster-justify-content--component` | `flex-start`  |
| `--cluster-align-items--component` 	 | `center`      |

```html
<div class="l-cluster"
	style="
		--cluster-space--component: var(--s-1);
		--cluster-justify-content--component: flex-start;
		--cluster-align-items--component: center;"
	>
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	<span class="item">Item</span>
	...
</div>
```

<PropSelect options={space_options} name="--cluster-space--component" bind:value={clusterSpace} />
<PropSelect options={justify_content_options} name="--cluster-justify-content--component" bind:value={clusterJustifyContent} />
<PropSelect options={align_items_options} name="--cluster-align-items--component" bind:value={clusterAlignItems} />

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-cluster" style={`
		--cluster-space--component: ${clusterSpace};
		--cluster-justify-content--component: ${clusterJustifyContent}; 
		--cluster-align-items--component: ${clusterAlignItems};
		`}>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item item--short">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item item--short">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item item--short">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Use as list

```html
<ul class="l-cluster">
	<li>List item</li>
	<li>List item</li>
	<li>List item</li>
	...
</ul>
```

<SqueezeContainer>
	<ul class="l-cluster">
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
	</ul>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Stack of lists

```html
<div class="l-stack">
	<ul class="l-cluster">
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		...
	</ul>
	<ul class="l-cluster">
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		...
	</ul>
</div>
```

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-stack">
		<ul class="l-cluster">
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
		</ul>
		<ul class="l-cluster">
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Two clusters combined

```html
<div class="l-cluster">
	<span class="item item--outer">Outer item</span>
	<div class="l-cluster">
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		<li class="item">List item</li>
		...
	</div>
</div>
```

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-cluster">
		<span class="item item--outer">Outer item</span>
		<div class="l-cluster">
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
			<li class="item">List item</li>
		</div>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## With a flex grow child element

Here a child element with the class `.u-flex-grow` applied will will have a `flex-grow` property of 1 - causing it to grow to stretch horizontally to fill the available space.

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-cluster">
		<span class="item u-flex-grow">.u-flex-grow</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
		<span class="item">Item</span>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## With focusable child elements

Using flexbox and the gap property ensures that the focus ring will not be clipped, as can happen when using negative margins.

```html
<div class="l-cluster">
	<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
	<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
	<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
	...
</div>
```

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-cluster">
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
		<a class="item" href="#">Item</a>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>